<section class="section-white" aria-labelledby="options-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="fade-up" style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow">Sedation &amp; Anesthesia Options</span>
      <h2 id="options-heading" class="section-heading">Levels of Comfort for Every Patient</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid-2x2" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);">
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Local Anesthesia</h3>
        <p>The foundation of any dental procedure. Precisely administered to numb the treatment area. You remain awake and aware, but the area is completely comfortable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Nitrous Oxide</h3>
        <p>Inhaled through a small nasal mask, nitrous oxide induces a relaxed, calm state. Effects wear off quickly once removed — you can typically drive yourself home.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>IV Sedation</h3>
        <p>Given through an IV by a board-certified MD anesthesiologist. You're deeply relaxed and breathing on your own, and most patients remember little of the procedure. Requires a driver home.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>General Anesthesia</h3>
        <p>You're fully asleep for the entire procedure, administered and monitored by a board-certified MD anesthesiologist. Often chosen for full-arch surgery and longer cases. Requires a driver home and pre-op instructions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-up" style="margin-top:var(--space-xl);padding:var(--space-xl);background:var(--ivory);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);">
      <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.75rem);margin-bottom:var(--space-sm);">Why an MD Anesthesiologist</h3>
      <p>When you choose IV sedation or general anesthesia, a board-certified MD anesthesiologist is in the room for your entire procedure. Their only job is your comfort and safety — monitoring your breathing, heart rate, and oxygen from start to finish — so Dr. Pasicznyk can focus completely on your surgery.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

