      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>IV sedation and general anesthesia are commonly chosen by patients with dental anxiety — but they are also practical for lengthy procedures, a strong gag reflex, or anyone who simply wants the procedure behind them without being aware of it.</p>
